WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
First-time users had no onboarding, so I added one with short copy and dots to go back.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:14.900
Instead of a group chat, a game room shows time, place, cost and who’s playing before you join.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:22.000
Testers had no clear moment to rate, so now a rating screen opens when a game ends.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.800
Level mattered more than knowing someone, so you can filter games by sport, skill and time.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.300
Testers asked about player numbers and drop-outs, so I added player limits and a waitlist.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.900
A good match should be easy to repeat, so your favourite playmates are one tap away.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.900
Profiles show skill, ratings and why someone plays, so you can trust them before you meet.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:49.200
After a test round, Settings left the tab bar and now opens from the profile menu.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.000
I chose a visible reliability star over a private warning, so others can decide who to trust.
